WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
This incidentally, is why

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Hollywood is making lots and lots of sequels

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Because there's two things by a chap called William Goldman who wrote books about movies. He also wrote the screenplay to two very famous movies, The Princess Bride and

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid. And he said

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The important thing to know about movies is that nobody knows anything, so nobody knows which movies are going to be a hit

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.000
The other thing to know about movies is nothing is as cheap as a hit. So if you make a movie and it's a hit

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The money that you make from it is just

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Amazing compared to the amount of money that it cost.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:52.000
But those two things together result in movie companies ending up essentially trying to make the same movie over and over again

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Preferably with the same title and a number added on the end of it, because that is a much safer bet than actually just trying to do something completely new.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
And so by upping the bet, you're doing something like that

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Not quite the same, but you're doing something which is a sequel to what you've done up to that point. And so it's a much more informed bet.

